From: thor2002ro <thor2002ro@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Local: dt-bindings: media: describe H616/H618 VE DDR mode

Define one VE DDR field value for H616 and H618 codecs.
Keep reconstruction write mode under codec control.

Signed-off-by: thor2002ro <thor2002ro@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/allwinner,sun4i-a10-video-engine.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/allwinner,sun4i-a10-video-engine.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/allwinner,sun4i-a10-video-engine.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/allwinner,sun4i-a10-video-engine.yaml
@@ -56,6 +56,16 @@
           - description: register value for device
     description: Phandle to the device SRAM
 
+  allwinner,ve-ddr-mode:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    enum: [2, 3]
+    description: |
+      Select the VE_MODE DDR field value in bits 17:16 for all H616 and H618 codecs.
+      The driver preserves reconstruction write bit 20 and each codec's other controls.
+      These values describe VE access modes, not the installed DDR generation or RAM width.
+      H616 and H618 default to mode 2 when this property is absent.
+      This property does not configure SRAM routing or the external DRAM controller.
+
   iommus:
     minItems: 1
     maxItems: 2
@@ -97,6 +107,7 @@
         nvmem-cell-names: [ nvmem-cells ]
     else:
       properties:
+        allwinner,ve-ddr-mode: false
         iommus:
           maxItems: 1
         nvmem-cells: false
